{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S5 change 1861 patchset 4 pushed. Root-caused all 3 prior CI failures to a single design flaw: runtime was threaded through worker->review_and_vote, but ~6 existing tests stub review_and_vote WITHOUT a runtime kwarg -> TypeError swallowed by worker except -> nothing drains (masked locally by xdist; CI runs serial). Fix: worker call reverted byte-identical to main (review_and_vote(event, config=cfg, force=force)); composed runtime now forwarded INSIDE _review_and_vote via _resolve_review_runtime helper (below the stub seam). Helper extraction keeps _review_and_vote at C901<=15 (baseline new=0). app.py _worker reverted to (queue,cfg); unused LLMRuntime import removed. Serial validation: 241 passed (incl test_review_bot/retrigger/complexity) + 19 oracle. lint+typecheck green. Note: pre-commit hook needs venv on PATH (ambient mypy/ruff otherwise fail spuriously)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787076360217309001,"uuid":"3e40b602-ef13-4092-b82a-ed46b8606fcf"}